<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Netherland Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1614–1618</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The New Netherland Company was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> trading company chartered by the States General in 1614 with a monopoly of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> between latitudes 40 and 45 degrees north. It built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-nassau-gold-coast">Fort Nassau</a> on Castle Island near present-day Albany. Its charter expired in 1618, and from 1621 the trade passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a>, which organised the colony of New Netherland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-netherland-company.jpg" alt="New Netherland Company" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adriaen Block · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wpdms_aq_block_1614.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
